Purpose: verify Phase 4 EX-stage forwarding for ALU operands, branch compare operands, JALR base operands, and x0 suppression.
Memory model: instruction memory has 1-cycle read latency; the testcase itself does not access data memory.
Hazard policy: no NOP spacing is inserted for the dependencies covered by forwarding.

Instruction flow:
1. addi x1, x0, 1 produces x1.
2. addi x2, x1, 2 immediately consumes x1 through EX/MEM forwarding.
3. add x3, x2, x1 consumes x2 from EX/MEM and x1 from MEM/WB.
4. add x4, x3, x2 consumes the newest matching values from EX/MEM and MEM/WB.
5. add x5, x0, x4 confirms rs2 forwarding into the ALU.
6. addi x0, x0, 99 followed by add x6, x0, x0 confirms writes to x0 are not forwarded.
7. addi x7, x0, 10 and addi x8, x7, 0 create branch operands without spacing.
8. beq x8, x7 is taken only if branch compare uses forwarded operands.
9. addi x9, x0, 99 is the wrong-path branch instruction and must be flushed.
10. addi x9, x0, 9 confirms execution resumes at the branch target.
11. addi x12, x0, 0x40 produces the JALR base immediately before JALR.
12. jalr x13, x12, 0 uses the forwarded base, jumps to 0x40, and writes link 0x38.
13. addi x14, x0, 99 and addi x15, x0, 77 are wrong-path JALR instructions and must be flushed.
14. addi x14, x0, 14 confirms execution resumes at the JALR target.
15. addi x15, x0, 20; addi x16, x0, 3; add x17, x15, x16 covers MEM/WB plus EX/MEM bypass in one ALU instruction.
16. addi x18, x17, 1 consumes the immediately preceding ALU result.

Expected output:
x0=00000000 x1=00000001 x2=00000003 x3=00000004 x4=00000007 x5=00000007
x6=00000000 x7=0000000a x8=0000000a x9=00000009
x12=00000040 x13=00000038 x14=0000000e x15=00000014
x16=00000003 x17=00000017 x18=00000018
